      "message": "I would propose doing this in a way that leaves all the string building work to the formatting function:\n\n```c++\n// Example: AUGMENT_LOG(I, \"hello!\");\n// Example: AUGMENT_LOG(W, \"value: %d\", value);\n#define AUGMENT_LOG(lfn, ...)                                           \\\n    ALOG##lfn(\"%s %s::%s \" __android_second(0, __VA_ARGS__, \"\"),        \\\n            mInstance.c_str(), getClassName().c_str(), __func__ __android_rest(__VA_ARGS__))\n// Example: AUGMENT_LOG_IF(D, value \u003c 0, \"negative\");\n// Example: AUGMENT_LOG_IF(E, value \u003c 0, \"bad value: %d\", value);\n#define AUGMENT_LOG_IF(lfn, cond, ...)                                  \\\n    ALOG##lfn##_IF(cond, \"%s %s::%s \" __android_second(0, __VA_ARGS__, \"\"), \\\n            mInstance.c_str(), getClassName().c_str(), __func__ __android_rest(__VA_ARGS__))\n// Used to register an entry into the function\n#define LOG_ENTRY() ALOGD(\"%s %s::%s\", mInstance.c_str(), getClassName().c_str(), __func__)\n```",
